      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-evidential-reasoning-01",
        "text": {
          "en": "The evidential basis differs across the claims: one rests on direct records, another on recollection, and a third on inference."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "پایه شواهد برای ادعاها یکسان نیست: یکی روی اسناد مستقیمه، یکی روی خاطره و سومی روی استنباط."
        },
        "intent": "classify_evidence_basis",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_evidential_reasoning_evidential",
          "c2_evidential_reasoning_attribution"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_evidential_reasoning_warrant",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-evidential-reasoning-01",
        "text": {
          "en": "The data warrant saying demand increased; they do not warrant saying the campaign caused the increase."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "داده‌ها اجازه می‌دن بگیم تقاضا بالا رفته، ولی اجازه نمی‌دن بگیم کمپین باعث اون افزایش شده."
        },
        "intent": "match_claim_to_warrant",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_evidential_reasoning_warrant",
          "c2_evidential_reasoning_certainty"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_evidential_reasoning_corroboration",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-evidential-reasoning-02",
        "text": {
          "en": "The anonymous account gains credibility because several details receive independent corroboration from records created at the time."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "روایت ناشناس معتبرتر می‌شه چون چند جزئیش با اسناد مستقلی که همون زمان ساخته شدن تأیید می‌شن."
        },
        "intent": "use_corroboration",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_evidential_reasoning_corroboration",
          "c2_evidential_reasoning_triangulate"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_evidential_reasoning_provisional",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-evidential-reasoning-02",
        "text": {
          "en": "My conclusion is provisional: it is the best fit for the current evidence, not a claim that alternatives have been eliminated."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "نتیجه‌م موقته: بهترین توضیح برای شواهد فعلیه، نه ادعای اینکه همه گزینه‌های دیگه حذف شدن."
        },
        "intent": "state_provisional_judgment",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_evidential_reasoning_provisional",
          "c2_evidential_reasoning_certainty"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_evidential_reasoning_triangulate",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-evidential-reasoning-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "Before treating the pattern as established, I would triangulate the survey with behavioral data and a source that does not share the same incentives."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "قبل از اینکه الگو رو قطعی بدونم، نظرسنجی رو با داده رفتاری و منبعی که منافع مشابهی نداره تطبیق می‌دم."
        },
        "intent": "triangulate_sources",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_evidential_reasoning_triangulate",
          "c2_evidential_reasoning_evidential"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_evidential_reasoning_indeterminate",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-evidential-reasoning-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "On motive, the evidence remains indeterminate; several explanations fit equally well."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "درباره انگیزه، شواهد هنوز نامشخصن؛ چند توضیح به یک اندازه با داده‌ها جور درمیاد."
        },
        "intent": "mark_indeterminacy",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_evidential_reasoning_indeterminate",
          "c2_evidential_reasoning_certainty"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_evidential_reasoning_attribution",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-evidential-reasoning-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "Careful attribution lets us report a serious claim without silently adopting the source's level of certainty as our own."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "نسبت دادن دقیق به منبع اجازه می‌ده یک ادعای جدی رو گزارش کنیم بدون اینکه میزان قطعیت منبع رو بی‌صدا مال خودمون کنیم."
        },
        "intent": "attribute_claim",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_evidential_reasoning_attribution",
          "c2_evidential_reasoning_provisional"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_evidential_reasoning_summary",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-evidential-reasoning-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "The disciplined position is neither skepticism about everything nor confidence by default; commitment should rise with the quality of the warrant."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "موضع دقیق نه شک به همه‌چیزه و نه اعتماد پیش‌فرض؛ میزان تعهد به ادعا باید با کیفیت پشتوانه‌اش بالا بره."
        },
        "intent": "calibrate_commitment",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_evidential_reasoning_warrant",
          "c2_evidential_reasoning_certainty"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c2_evidential_reasoning_advanced_reporting",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-evidential-reasoning-01",
        "slug": "c2-evidential-reasoning-advanced-reporting",
        "title": "Advanced reporting verbs",
        "rule_summary": "Choose reporting verbs such as acknowledge, maintain, concede, dispute, imply, and caution to represent a source's stance accurately.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "برای بازتاب دقیق موضع منبع از فعل‌هایی مثل acknowledge، maintain، concede، dispute، imply و caution استفاده می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The author acknowledges the limitation but maintains that the trend is meaningful.",
            "fa": "نویسنده محدودیت را می‌پذیرد اما همچنان معتقد است روند معنادار است."
          },
          {
            "en": "The report cautions against treating correlation as proof of cause.",
            "fa": "گزارش هشدار می‌دهد همبستگی را به‌عنوان اثبات علت در نظر نگیریم."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c2_evidential_reasoning_advanced_hedging",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-evidential-reasoning-02",
        "slug": "c2-evidential-reasoning-advanced-hedging",
        "title": "Advanced hedging and calibration",
        "rule_summary": "Calibrate certainty with expressions such as arguably, broadly speaking, tends to, appears to, and cannot entirely be ruled out.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "در C1 میزان قطعیت را با عبارت‌هایی مثل arguably، broadly speaking، tends to، appears to و cannot entirely be ruled out دقیق تنظیم می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The change appears to have improved access, although the evidence is still limited.",
            "fa": "به نظر می‌رسد این تغییر دسترسی را بهتر کرده، هرچند شواهد هنوز محدود است."
          },
          {
            "en": "That explanation cannot entirely be ruled out.",
            "fa": "نمی‌توان آن توضیح را کاملاً منتفی دانست."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c2_evidential_reasoning_reporting_passive",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-evidential-reasoning-03",
        "slug": "c2-evidential-reasoning-reporting-passive",
        "title": "Impersonal reporting structures",
        "rule_summary": "Use structures such as is thought to, is believed to, and has been reported to when the source is general or deliberately backgrounded.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "وقتی منبع عمومی است یا عمداً در پس‌زمینه قرار می‌گیرد از ساختارهایی مثل is thought to، is believed to و has been reported to استفاده می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The policy is thought to have reduced short-term demand.",
            "fa": "گمان می‌رود این سیاست تقاضای کوتاه‌مدت را کاهش داده باشد."
          },
          {
            "en": "The company is reported to be reconsidering the plan.",
            "fa": "گزارش شده شرکت در حال بازنگری برنامه است."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c2_evidential_reasoning_scene_1",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-evidential-reasoning-01",
        "title": "Evidential Reasoning & Degrees of Commitment: part 1",
        "setting": "professional workshop",
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "characters": [
          "Nora",
          "Samir"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Nora",
            "text": "How would you respond without making the disagreement personal?",
            "translation_fa": "چطور جواب می‌دادی بدون اینکه مخالفت شخصی بشه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Samir",
            "text": "The evidential basis differs across the claims: one rests on direct records, another on recollection, and a third on inference.",
            "translation_fa": "پایه شواهد برای ادعاها یکسان نیست: یکی روی اسناد مستقیمه، یکی روی خاطره و سومی روی استنباط."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Nora",
            "text": "What could you concede while still holding your position?",
            "translation_fa": "چی رو می‌تونی بپذیری و در عین حال موضعت رو حفظ کنی؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 4,
            "speaker": "Samir",
            "text": "The data warrant saying demand increased; they do not warrant saying the campaign caused the increase.",
            "translation_fa": "داده‌ها اجازه می‌دن بگیم تقاضا بالا رفته، ولی اجازه نمی‌دن بگیم کمپین باعث اون افزایش شده."
          }
        ],
        "status": "approved"
      }
